---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const path = '/methodology/';
const author = siteConfig.author;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology & Correction Log | DocuForge"
  description="How DocuForge Tools are built: sources policy, what templates leave out, AI disclosure, changelog, and correction log. Maintained by Hammad Iqbal."
  path={path}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Methodology', path }]} />
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This page explains how I produce the generators and educational copy on {siteConfig.siteName},
    what the tools leave out, and how I correct mistakes. Maintained by {author.name}.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources policy</h2>
  <p>
    Tool pages cite primary public sources relevant to the document type—for example IRS pages on
    independent contractors and recordkeeping, Cornell LII Wex/CFR definitions, SBA small-business
    guides, HUD fair-housing and rental pages, CDC infection-control overviews, the U.S. Copyright
    Office’s photographer materials, and FTC small-business / endorsement guidance. I link the final
    URL I checked. I do not invent statutes or pretend a page was attorney-reviewed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each tool’s <strong>Sources</strong> list says what the citation is used for and the date I last
    checked it. “Last reviewed” on a page changes only when the formula, sources, or substantive
    text actually change—not to look fresh.
  </p>

  <h2>What the tools leave out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Jurisdiction-specific statutory language (state landlord-tenant codes, local tattoo regs, etc.).</li>
    <li>Tax advice, filing obligations, or employer/contractor classification determinations.</li>
    <li>Attorney review, notarization, e-sign compliance, or enforceability guarantees.</li>
    <li>Server-side storage of your filled documents—exports stay on your device.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How a generator works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sample defaults render in the HTML as a static preview (indexable, useful before JavaScript).</li>
    <li>The interactive editor loads on demand; validation and live preview run in your browser.</li>
    <li>PDF/DOCX engines load only when you export.</li>
    <li>Optional drafts use <code>localStorage</code> under a per-tool key—never uploaded to our servers.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>AI / automation disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Drafts may be written with AI assistance. Every formula, sample default, and reference link is
    checked by {author.name} against the sources listed on each page before publication.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changelog">Changelog</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Date</th>
          <th scope="col">Change</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time></td>
          <td>
            Mobile SEO audit fixes: editor loader bundling, TrustBlock authorship, playbook favicon
            set, sample HTML previews, IRS/LII/SBA source list, Edit/Preview mobile tabs.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><time datetime="2026-10-19">2026-10-19</time></td>
          <td>Initial public launch of sixteen document generators on workers.dev.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="corrections">Correction log</h2>
  <p>
    Confirmed factual fixes will be listed here with the date, page, and what changed. Removing an
    unsupported “editorial team” or “reviewed by” claim counts as a correction.
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Date</th>
          <th scope="col">Correction</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time></td>
          <td>
            Removed anonymous “DocuForge Editorial / Review Team” authorship. Site is maintained by
            {author.name} alone; there is no separate reviewer. Added honest About and Methodology pages.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with the page,
    what looks wrong, and a source URL. See also <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
